{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7EGDsvatMoghdvWru3Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I draft, a few questions. Your answers will decide how the speech handles the hardest parts.\n\n1. **What's the main objection you expect tonight?** Is it traffic on Alder, parking spillover, density, or something else? And do you know whether the commissioners themselves have raised any concerns? Three minutes only covers one objection properly, so I want to pick the right one.\n2. **Is anything planned to fix the Alder and 4th intersection?** For example, retimed signals, a turn lane, or a condition of approval. If not, I'll address the C-to-D drop honestly rather than skip it. Someone else will bring it up if you don't.\n3. **Is there a personal story you'd be comfortable telling?** For example, someone you know who is on the waiting list or who was priced out of the area, or what you've seen of Alder Road over 19 years. One real person usually lands better than a fourth statistic.\n4. **What exactly is the commission voting on tonight?** Is it a rezoning, a variance, a site plan or something else? And are you asking them to approve it as proposed or with conditions? The closing ask should match the decision in front of them.\n5. **Do you want to say up front that you're a member of the church?** I'd recommend it, since commissioners or opponents may already know and it builds trust to say it first. But it's your call.\n\nIf you don't know some of these, that's fine. I'll write without them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":379,"cache_read_input_tokens":9532,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":379},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null